<title>PORTUGAL: Bank/Portugal may have intervened on escudo/mark.</title>
<headline>Bank/Portugal may have intervened on escudo/mark.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Portugal may have intervened  during the afternoon to steady the escudo, selling marks at around  101.10 escudos, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Portuguese currency remained under slight pressure at the close  of European trade, being quoted at 101.10/13 against its 101.05/08  opening. The Bank action was seemingly aimed at stopping the currency  slipping to 101.15, some traders said.</p>
<p>But traders said the market lacked depth with players more interested  in movements in the dollar and sterling.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
